messages:
sam: Heads-up — trying to get the JS SDK working in an Expo dev client (Hermes). Metro ends up bundling the ESM entry and app crashes: global.crypto undefined + ReadableStream missing. Any lightweight fixes?

ilya: Yep. Metro respects `exports.import` which will point to dist/index.mjs if that's how the SDK is published. Short term: force CJS.

sam: Can you show the package.json exports pattern? Ours is `{ "exports": { "./": { "import": "dist/index.mjs", "require": "dist/index.cjs" } } }` so Metro picks the import entry.

nadia: Two practical approaches: 1) add a metro resolver alias to the CJS file, 2) import CJS directly with `const SDK = require('my-sdk/dist/index.cjs')`.

chris: At runtime you'll still need polyfills for RN/Hermes: `react-native-get-random-values`, an `AbortController` polyfill, and a ReadableStream ponyfill. Hermes also sometimes needs `Symbol.asyncIterator` shim.

sam: Example metro alias we used:```js
// metro.config.js
const path = require('path')
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      'my-sdk$': path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules/my-sdk/dist/index.cjs')
    }
  }
}
```

ilya: Minimal app entry shims:```js
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
import 'abortcontroller-polyfill/dist/abortcontroller-polyfill-only';
const { ReadableStream } = require('web-streams-polyfill/ponyfill');
if (!global.ReadableStream) global.ReadableStream = ReadableStream;
if (!Symbol.asyncIterator) Symbol.asyncIterator = Symbol.for('asyncIterator');
```

nadia: TypeScript will likely complain because SDK types import `node:stream`. We set `skipLibCheck: true` temporarily and added a tiny `declare module 'node:stream'` shim in our app to silence it. Not ideal.

chris: Long-term asks to open with the SDK maintainers: 1) add `react-native` field or make `main` point to a CJS RN-friendly build, 2) ensure `exports` includes a require fallback packagers can use, 3) publish a small browser/UMD bundle that omits Node-only runtime bits, 4) split or conditionally emit types that don't import `node:` libs, 5) add an `examples/expo` sample prewired with shims.

sam: I'll open the issue and attach a tiny repro (expo prebuild + Hermes). What should I include?

ilya: Include Metro logs showing it picked dist/index.mjs, the Hermes runtime stack trace (global.crypto/ReadableStream errors), and a tsconfig + tsc output showing the type errors. Small repro app + steps to repro is great.

nadia: Also paste the minimal metro snippet and the shim code in the issue so devs can copy/paste. Mention Expo SDK 48+ has `crypto.getRandomValues` in managed runtimes — dev clients still need polyfills for older versions.

expo-bot: Note: Expo SDK 48+ surfaces `crypto.getRandomValues` in managed runtimes; custom dev clients and older SDKs may still require polyfills. See https://blog.expo.dev/ for details.

chris: For immediate unblock feel free to ping me; I have a small helper repo that automates the alias + shims to get a demo running. We can attach that to the issue.

sam: Awesome — I'll draft the GH issue now and include the repro, the checklist (metro alias or require CJS, polyfills, tsconfig skipLibCheck) and request items above. Thanks all :thumbsup:
